{"objects":[{"id":"flow","instance":"instance--b96dad5f-c519-5a1f-a718-912ca4a86c02","objects":["attack-action--1","attack-action--2","attack-action--3","attack-action--4","attack-action--5","attack-condition--1","attack-condition--2","attack-operator--1","software--1","file--1","instance--33d457be-25c6-5663-82ef-1321ce9b6639","instance--db0beeef-7a6d-5300-a4f5-0d87a3a707c7","directory--1","directory--2","directory--3","instance--183f0ea4-2466-5bd9-b5e6-654dbd28e66d","instance--b03f7f6c-1596-53a3-9508-69157de01fbe","instance--ffef9c83-92da-5621-888d-bdc7082e09e0","instance--46e1f5ca-0ea1-5df1-b1a9-3318b621fdc4","instance--1fa25a2c-eb73-5639-9fc1-fcc3c0b30784","file--4","process--2","instance--ad1f125b-7701-5e9d-b869-79f40471648d","instance--dba76cba-ac10-53fc-8651-9c93dbcacdf3","instance--ed6039fe-678b-5ae9-9576-73e6ea35b0c8","instance--d10376f5-8e18-5fa1-93e0-8fa9e55f61b1","instance--56da8838-1109-5fce-9d89-7b3ec32d7010","instance--714f6cb9-bdb0-5e83-914a-3c8158d9f2de","instance--d110b130-8c28-5cb4-98a0-76aaa8233093","instance--f64caa83-12dd-5204-a53f-519db6b69a9d","instance--5c474795-7a46-5c6c-af4d-203928d704a3","instance--d3cd91c5-fb45-5a59-b4e0-4bb5609961ab","instance--4fbde158-28da-551a-89d1-9a78d69d8882","instance--7c658664-6d38-5a13-88bd-6c23e6130fdf","instance--8c95d2c3-f09d-5a1b-96cc-f220bbbd9d95","instance--45c9bcab-c516-5a62-ac2f-1b068db266e0","instance--b98b21c5-4e8c-51e8-af90-665bb9d3abcd","instance--3dbdf34c-21b5-5621-b0ac-cd96aea7ab09","instance--585534a6-ac03-5265-9706-c244742a0e53","instance--149e66dd-f433-5e8f-bb4e-748cec2238ff","instance--0676e98c-0b6d-5bb9-9a89-846c76a7a797","instance--3df441b6-1dcd-5d25-b855-b8e2d42eafa5","instance--1fafad58-6a22-5ace-938c-20e4da6f0345"],"properties":[["name","Lazarus DLL side-loading and in-memory payload execution"],["description","While tracking the Lazarus attack group, the ASEC analysis team discovered that the attackers were using the DLL Side-Loading attack technique (T1574.002) by abusing legitimate applications in the initial compromise stage to achieve the next stage of their attack process."],["scope","incident"],["author",[["name","AhnLab ASEC"]]],["external_references",[["item-1",[["source_name","asec.ahnlab.com"],["url","https://asec.ahnlab.com/en/39828/"]]]]]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ad592d05-6969-5b51-98a8-1ad9b6aab896","120":"instance--5850a8f4-8241-5e73-9bf0-dcd376cd5025","150":"instance--0da1498f-3beb-5916-a249-e0410a4a81e4","180":"instance--d3632784-7391-5a29-83e2-edab51db56c6","210":"instance--8bc47ca5-ca73-5a04-a9ea-918608f10871","240":"instance--6546eef6-c5ad-516e-a417-89916e651648","270":"instance--244e5a69-f465-564e-9d2c-93d4da44fc57","30":"instance--6a1fca3c-fdb6-536a-bbea-61ac2349a700","300":"instance--043a5b44-2864-5565-abce-1909204e5485","330":"instance--e10eb918-2b0b-56f4-9c82-f345ce21276c","60":"instance--33a99d1b-dad8-51f6-be74-e1614db9151b","90":"instance--380c79e9-b1eb-547c-bf01-a011db1201c1"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--1","properties":[["name","Distribute initial backdoor via Initech process"],["description","According to AhnLab\u2019s ASD (AhnLab Smart Defense) infrastructure, the attackers used an old version of the Initech process (inisafecrosswebexsvc.exe) through which they distributed the backdoor malware (scskapplink.dll) used for the initial compromise."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1218"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--4f4d03a8-4502-5010-997b-9943e254395b","120":"instance--cefe62ac-5b6e-5ead-84fc-b4c632913a73","150":"instance--4d07a740-2467-5b95-ac8d-4a2ee8edd11e","180":"instance--1205f03c-a457-5a0b-87ef-3bbb7aac110f","210":"instance--96e7dc6a-9f86-5f69-8d45-a566303cd4c0","240":"instance--66237af6-bb19-5a51-9fa2-cbc4a96186f5","270":"instance--836dfd42-b475-50ca-9acf-4f11bd32b89f","30":"instance--efe92997-cc5c-538a-90bc-c09ffb1379f4","300":"instance--9c4a24ae-1426-5cb5-9d7c-792e6dd325b7","330":"instance--06c6a74a-ca7d-5703-88ea-a06a0933d21a","60":"instance--5e4f84e5-56b7-5b8f-9bc3-b4d59d371123","90":"instance--019deb6a-bab3-57db-9a53-11e3564bf7a4"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--2","properties":[["name","Create wsmprovhost side-loading files"],["description","Afterward, it is likely that the executed backdoor malware created wsmprovhost.exe and executed an additional DLL Side-Loading payload. The grounds for the suspected use of the DLL Side-Loading technique lie in the fact that an additional malicious DLL named \u201cmi.dll\u201d was found in the folder path where wsmprovhost.exe was created in the infected PCs. The following is the file path information of mi.dll that was in the same path as wsmprovhost.exe.\n\nC:\\ProgramData\\Microsoft\\IdentityCRL\\mi.dll\n\nC:\\ProgramData\\Microsoft\\IdentityCRL\\wsmprovhost.exe\n\nC:\\ProgramData\\USOShared\\mi.dll\n\nC:\\ProgramData\\USOShared\\wsmprovhost.exe\n\nC:\\ProgramData\\midassoft\\mi.dll\n\nC:\\ProgramData\\midassoft\\wsmprovhost.exe"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1574.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0ce35aea-35a2-52ae-a67b-985306bdefe7","120":"instance--312639d5-e6d9-57b1-850d-28f0a1eac2f6","150":"instance--9551a25e-2558-512e-9894-dd64a8d662bf","180":"instance--403becce-e0ad-5dcd-bc14-7c00453907da","210":"instance--2305f501-2712-5ec6-9d4e-1371b011e937","240":"instance--cf1b8cf6-1cbd-5afb-b653-aa693889dab5","270":"instance--1d3dc59a-40a0-5670-aa3e-1304ff762003","30":"instance--77063d4f-503a-5e9b-b622-15aa2cc6a8e7","300":"instance--beaab67f-8a54-5982-8c5d-9d2ed2d42c9f","330":"instance--4d3274ff-ef14-5a53-99be-01575194a98e","60":"instance--4154a6bf-290b-5fce-a557-5dc0f3e700fb","90":"instance--2992bc0b-df57-54e5-a17b-03a964338c09"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--3","properties":[["name","Run wsmprovhost to load mi.dll"],["description","mi.dll is a DLL referenced by wsmprovhost.exe (See Figure 3). Thus, when wsmprovhost.exe is run, mi.dll is loaded in the corresponding process memory."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1574.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0f6e4da7-a5f4-54d7-866f-3bc6e8bcb019","120":"instance--015254b5-0906-577e-b3e3-3899f837d118","150":"instance--f7af5b8c-330a-58d5-b0da-a3d5f0bc6ad0","180":"instance--9f27ab21-2382-567d-b022-74ad5a29bd08","210":"instance--d799eb0a-7600-5b1a-a298-c47a78ceae4b","240":"instance--911c2c52-5974-5e08-b0b6-a9084d57c6ee","270":"instance--286444b4-97a1-58cd-9ca3-cffa04a15351","30":"instance--92192c38-5143-50e0-8c39-a96ea86e32e2","300":"instance--82bb3de0-bea5-5651-a1de-583283258c6d","330":"instance--4f0945c8-f644-50ce-8796-fea52a29dda1","60":"instance--16c43a2d-7356-521d-a507-5922e2c3337b","90":"instance--abce5c62-339a-5ed5-a0b8-dd66136cfe2f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--4","properties":[["name","Decrypt embedded binary and execute in memory"],["description","The malicious mi.dll that is executed in the process memory of wsmprovhost.exe includes an additional binary encrypted internally with the AES-128 algorithm, and the moment it is executed, it uses the decryption key transmitted via an argument to decrypt the binary before running an additional malware in the memory."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1055"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--a469636c-0cb2-50b9-92f9-644c8aa98197","120":"instance--d57b3a21-e910-5879-8148-40165cea451a","150":"instance--58250ef4-5bb4-5bf3-b33e-89493bbb395d","180":"instance--3e769cf2-c1e5-5d2e-81d4-892f48ce4d86","210":"instance--f6499e41-749c-5d7f-9346-96c08d0d5dfd","240":"instance--d9dcdfc8-5f42-546a-803a-0efcd5d4cf91","270":"instance--c9afd0f6-97ce-57b2-9d60-3557b6214809","30":"instance--75f82155-f5ff-5619-8bf8-aae22937cab0","300":"instance--25e2d26e-1b35-56bd-b9aa-096c2d3b0e3c","330":"instance--e0483688-da10-5376-8cf2-050bcc3b70f0","60":"instance--1293d9cc-16b2-5c67-a453-bd144aab133a","90":"instance--2b43cd52-10db-5b15-8ad5-c4b59496528b"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--5","properties":[["name","Execute malware via dfrgui.exe"],["description","It has also been identified that the Lazarus group not only executed malware through wsmprovhost.exe but also other normal Windows programs such as dfrgui.exe. Using a DLL that is run in a normal process memory area to perform malicious acts is deemed to be an attempt to bypass the behavior detection of security software."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1574.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--35652c79-2c41-5d60-81ba-b5e47aa554bf","120":"instance--53906203-fffb-5af3-b112-44a9b4b49b8f","150":"instance--465fbc8a-7b4c-569f-be00-c0fbc137fcfc","180":"instance--a653c96b-3673-5dfa-968e-188fffe4cc04","210":"instance--6a344cf5-bd5c-52db-84f5-23c7701c7a5e","30":"instance--913561d1-b5f3-54d2-8272-159233dfde54","330":"instance--d59fe52d-c897-5f3a-919a-c2273cb8a8b3","60":"instance--f1fd6a3d-bb83-543d-a379-39d4632978f7","90":"instance--4cd6fce2-0d24-57f0-b161-12a867cd1100","branch:False":"instance--f7e897b3-3607-5ea5-8d15-5f83ba8a60da","branch:True":"instance--39b5ac19-b0dd-5674-a7d9-d75e659fe9ea"},"id":"condition","instance":"attack-condition--1","properties":[["description","Afterward, it is likely that the executed backdoor malware created wsmprovhost.exe and executed an additional DLL Side-Loading payload."]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--2ff8b105-17d8-5bc8-9736-a71ca9281068","120":"instance--fe9b11f7-9a07-51c8-93b2-02f34148833b","150":"instance--15f0676c-2f2f-58cf-99a3-b5eade2d286e","180":"instance--cdc5e3d9-a0b4-5995-98a3-d1a29532ffb1","210":"instance--75ed5df8-ff2f-5667-9748-b8587a1ee318","30":"instance--46009917-4258-54e5-9e91-c46c4a45d34d","330":"instance--54845373-a5f0-5af0-b348-5b0a3b4fbe67","60":"instance--f1f8d9a5-1f2a-55c4-af9a-f2629bc0827a","90":"instance--ddfb6e54-4af9-5771-910f-b4c7ba6e9860","branch:False":"instance--64607b7d-a4bd-56e7-9116-7bc21201c8bf","branch:True":"instance--f635d174-aa29-531f-b9c8-0cc481c6c1dd"},"id":"condition","instance":"attack-condition--2","properties":[["description","mi.dll is a DLL referenced by wsmprovhost.exe (See Figure 3). Thus, when wsmprovhost.exe is run, mi.dll is loaded in the corresponding process memory."]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--36aad375-d405-5e3b-9a7d-4346c75c9f45","120":"instance--acc72955-e581-59b3-80b5-35fb047df4b8","150":"instance--d5d0ec7c-da1b-5d39-86e4-8de8792ab05d","180":"instance--047e7862-d9c4-5716-b778-899a86595b48","210":"instance--650a6d3c-5cb0-5f82-83ec-c5d828e2502b","240":"instance--3f08654d-fd5e-59cb-af47-8bbcee29de39","270":"instance--e175549d-38ff-5527-bdb8-de5e1a12f356","30":"instance--c6e60459-b005-50cd-9e68-66ef210b5456","300":"instance--f90b34f0-8620-5a56-9e11-4db2b889aac4","330":"instance--93872aee-cf81-52fa-aa93-f7a84a833dbd","60":"instance--5a877a06-3649-5bba-9461-5faee75ea842","90":"instance--68af6616-0e27-5395-b4ff-5d95b55a2405"},"id":"AND_operator","instance":"attack-operator--1","properties":[["operator","AND"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--905f37ff-524a-522a-8685-08b6df9b34bd","120":"instance--a0b8bf42-8310-53d9-87f0-390378638ae9","150":"instance--ffafa2fa-6430-5714-9c5e-bbf977c9819b","180":"instance--10bf0e4d-ac4d-5742-b82b-398ef2467e2a","210":"instance--f2066b53-6fa4-5efa-8f61-dc81d3df5b0e","240":"instance--fbb6b151-c9f4-5cb6-b467-c563cc0c60d3","270":"instance--451ff5e8-5cc8-5d6c-b701-da17c04936f7","30":"instance--059bc992-da53-5d4b-ac82-60cfacc08e81","300":"instance--1d241382-a8ee-554a-aa3a-04366535b315","330":"instance--8a7078e9-787d-56b2-a734-f93cd76b3dc8","60":"instance--8aab1831-f6e3-582d-8f9b-3ad920a40e35","90":"instance--192458e5-76c8-5d8c-ab54-9ed8b36ef2bd"},"id":"software","instance":"software--1","properties":[["value","inisafecrosswebexsvc.exe"],["evidence",[["item-1",{"excerpt":"the attackers used an old version of the Initech process (inisafecrosswebexsvc.exe)","source":"https://asec.ahnlab.com/en/39828/","source_field":"normalized_text"}]]],["display_name","inisafecrosswebexsvc.exe"],["name","inisafecrosswebexsvc.exe"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--8cf549a5-7e7d-51cf-9368-9b5e0744592a","120":"instance--06d4fda8-e0bf-57